codex
I found a stop-the-line incompatibility in the accepted baseline: both manifest-v1 schemas intentionally preserve `additionalProperties: true`, and their only version gate forbids `runtime_roots`, `dependencies`, and `capabilities`. Therefore `build_roots` is currently valid under schema 1, while the acceptance criteria require it to be rejected and simultaneously forbid rewriting legacy schemas or changing schemas 1–5 semantics. I’m verifying this with the repository’s actual validator and checking whether there is an existing non-schema compatibility layer that resolves the contradiction before I mark it blocked.
